You translate a list of chapter / section headings for an academic book.

## Task
For each row below, produce a faithful, natural-sounding {{ target_language }}
translation of the heading. Output strict JSON only — no prose, no markdown
fences — matching this schema:

{
  "items": [
    { "section_id": "<id from input>", "translated": "<translated heading>" },
    ...
  ]
}

## Constraints
- Preserve any leading chapter number / roman numeral / "Chapter N" marker
  intact (e.g. "1 Grow" → "1 增长"; "Chapter III" → "第三章" is fine).
- Keep proper nouns / acronyms untouched unless they have an established
  {{ target_language }} translation (e.g. NATO → 北约).
- Match register: book chapter titles tend to be terse; do not over-explain.
- Do not paraphrase or summarize. Translate the heading text, not its content.
- If the heading is purely numeric (e.g. "1.1") or purely a proper noun that
  has no natural {{ target_language }} form, echo it back unchanged.
- The output MUST include exactly one item per input row, with `section_id`
  matching the input. Same order is preferred but not required.

## Book context (for register & terminology)
Title: {{ book_title }}
Thesis: {{ book_thesis }}

## Glossary (use these target terms when they appear in a heading)
{% for g in glossary %}- {{ g.term }} → {{ g.target }}
{% endfor %}

## Headings to translate
{% for h in headings %}- section_id={{ h.section_id }} | level={{ h.level }} | source={{ h.heading | tojson }}
{% endfor %}
